    characters and each chunk is encoded independently. In this case, the return value is a
    list of token lists, with one list of tokens per chunk.

    ```
    >>> enc.encode_ordinary("hello world")
    [31373, 995]
    >>> enc.encode_ordinary("hello world", chunk_size=6)
    [[31373, 220], [995]]
    ```
